{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Added a dated OSS reference set for all three RP-04 auth classes to .joe-janitor/rp04-secrets-research.md. Git evidence: git/git (62.6k stars), Git Credential Manager (9.2k), and GitHub CLI (45.9k) converge on URL-scoped external credential helpers, OAuth/keychain ownership, and separate CI environment-token mode. Pydantic/LLM evidence: PydanticAI (19.3k) directly accepts injected AsyncOpenAI, Anthropic, and boto3 Bedrock clients; the official OpenAI, Anthropic, and boto3 SDKs own workload identity, refresh/cache/invalidation, or AWS credential-chain behavior. Jira evidence: MCP Atlassian (5.7k) provides explicit Cloud API-token, DC PAT, mTLS, and OAuth modes and disables Requests trust_env for explicit PAT/OAuth; Airflow (46.5k) materializes a named Jira connection inside its Jira hook; jira-cli (5.9k) separates non-secret config from environment/netrc/keychain token material; pycontribs/jira exposes distinct Cloud basic_auth and DC token_auth constructors. All repositories were unarchived and pushed within the preceding week when checked 2026-08-16 PT. Gitleaks scanned the recovery artifacts after the update and found no leaks."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786936348307078001,"uuid":"68f746e3-bc23-43d9-b8a3-acf3e2c8774b"}